# Web Frontend (Next.js / React / Modern Web)

**Scope:** Dedicated web frontend workspaces (`web/`, `apps/web/`, `src/`). Mobile app work → **`mobile-flutter.mdc`** + **`rules.mdc`**. Shared schema/policies → central database migrations directory.

Cross-cutting rules still apply strictly: **`rules.mdc`**, **`git-commits.mdc`**, **`english-comments-only.mdc`**, **`engineering-quality.mdc`** (Windows `;`, no empty catches, strict types), **`interaction-ux.mdc`** (optimistic UI, skeletons, confirmations), and **`data-sync-and-security.mdc`**.

---

## Problem-Solving

- Deliver precise behavior with minimal focused diffs matching existing repository patterns.
- Choose the simplest React/Next.js architecture — prefer **Server Components** by default where supported, reserving `'use client'` for genuinely interactive leaves.
- Use **skeleton loaders** for list and feed fetches — never blank screens or full-page spinners when layout/chrome can stay visible.
- Completion replies: **2–3 words max** after the user-name prefix unless the user asked a question requiring explanation (see **`rules.mdc`**).

---

## Architecture

| Layer | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Routes / Pages | `src/app/` — thin `page.tsx` (~30–80 lines); compose panels and workspaces |
| Components | `src/components/` — `ui/`, `layout/`, `features/` (~150–250 lines max per panel; split earlier) |
| Data & API | `src/lib/<domain>/*-api.ts` + custom `use*` hooks — never 200-line data fetches inside JSX |
| State | Server state + hooks; minimal client stores (`src/stores/`) only where shared client state is required |
| Crypto / Heavy CPU | **Web Workers only** (`src/workers/`) — Web Crypto API; never block the main UI thread |
| Types | `src/types/` — strict TypeScript; zero `any` |

- **Platform separation:** Never expand legacy mobile-web fallbacks (`kIsWeb`) when a dedicated web frontend exists.
- **Naming:** `kebab-case` files; `PascalCase` components; `useX` hooks; `onX` callbacks.
- **Zero business logic in JSX:** Extract transformations, API orchestration, and formatting into `src/lib/` or custom hooks.

---

## UI, Design Tokens & i18n

- Consume all colors, surfaces, radii, and elevation strictly through semantic **CSS variables / design tokens** (e.g., `src/styles/tokens.css`) — never scatter raw brand hex values in feature components.
- Dark theme canvas uses semantic dark surface tokens — never pure black (`#000000`) except immersive fullscreen media viewers.
- Configure script-aware fonts (e.g., Arabic + Latin system/brand font stacks) and support light/dark/system themes seamlessly.
- Extend the shared layout primitives (`app-shell`, sidebars, top nav, mobile tab bar) — never fork duplicate shells.
- Mobile breakpoints: touch targets **≥ 44px**; always preserve visible `:focus-visible` keyboard rings.
- Virtualize long feeds, timelines, and tables when collections grow large.
- **i18n:** Route 100% of UI strings through the project's i18n dictionary/helper — **zero** hardcoded copy; keep locales (`en`, `ar`, etc.) and `dir` (`rtl`/`ltr`) synchronized, with `dir="auto"` for user-authored content.

---

## Backend, Auth & Security (Any Backend / Any DB)

- Use SSR-safe session clients and middleware refresh where SSR is enabled (e.g., `@supabase/ssr`, NextAuth/Auth.js, HTTP-only session cookies, or typed BFF endpoints).
- **Environment safety:** Only expose explicitly public client variables (e.g., `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`) to the browser — **never** expose service-role, admin, or private API keys in client bundles or git history.
- Enforce server-side authorization / Row-Level Security (RLS), paginate all list queries, and use tightly scoped/bounded realtime subscriptions.
- **NEVER** log auth tokens, passwords, plaintext messages, or private keys.
- Sanitize any user-supplied HTML/markdown before rendering and enforce Content Security Policy (CSP) headers.

---

## Cross-Platform Crypto & Sync Parity

- When sharing a backend with a mobile client, maintain strict **protocol parity** (cipher suite, key envelope, payload metadata, and `deleted_by`/reconciliation rules per **`data-sync-and-security.mdc`**).
- Decrypt visible messages/items lazily without stalling scroll; cache decrypted plaintext safely in **IndexedDB** with a versioned, cleanable schema.
- Run all cryptographic operations inside **Web Workers** using Web Crypto — avoid legacy main-thread libraries (`JSEncrypt`, synchronous crypto) for new code.

---

## Quality & Verification

- Run **`npm run lint`**, type checking (`tsc --noEmit`), and **`npm run build`** before finishing release-critical or multi-file changes.
- Windows PowerShell: chain commands with **`;`**, never **`&&`**.

## Critical Rules Summary

1. Keep web changes strictly inside the web frontend — never expand frozen mobile-web targets.
2. Centralized SSR/API auth + public env vars only — never hardcode or leak private keys.
3. Offload crypto to **Web Workers**; maintain exact protocol parity with mobile clients.
4. Semantic design tokens (`tokens.css`) for styling; skeletons for feeds; `dir="auto"` for user content.
5. Enforce server authorization/RLS, pagination, and bounded realtime; keep locales + RTL synchronized.
6. Server Components by default, thin route files, and business/data logic cleanly extracted to `lib/` + hooks.
7. Manage shared database schema, indexes, and access policies in the central migrations directory only.
